sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-memory-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Levin argues that the paradox that a changing agent or species ceases to be itself while an unchanging one dies out is resolved by continuous commitment to creative, adaptive confabulation (reinterpretation of memories and information) at levels from molecular to behavioural, in individuals and whole lineages.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adaptive confabulation resolves the persistence paradox for individuals and lineages";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Self-Improvising Memory: A Perspective on Memories as Agential, Dynamically Reinterpreting Cognitive Glue”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2024), doi:10.3390/e26060481; section “Abstract”. Scope: Individual organisms and evolutionary lineages"
}
